From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:52:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(kanban): assert review wall suppression evidence
 [daveey]

Why: review admission populated clock_held and respawn_guarded, but the
regression only asserted the clock mapping. Deleting the suppression append
therefore escaped the tests while dropping stuck/capacity held-card evidence.
Assert the exact suppression entry on every deferred dispatch across review
and ready lanes, deep and standard routes, and four wall/hold sources.

Proof: deleting the append gives 16 failed / 18 passed; restoring it gives
34 passed. scripts/check --base origin/main passes all guards.
---
 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_review_wall_admission.py | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_review_wall_admission.py b/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_review_wall_admission.py
index 7f8f654860..a4572cb1f1 100644
--- a/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_review_wall_admission.py
+++ b/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_review_wall_admission.py
@@ -47,6 +47,7 @@ def test_walled_review_not_claimed_and_unwalled_host_claims(
             res = dispatch.dispatch_once(conn, spawn_fn=lambda task, _ws: seen.append(task.id))
             assert seen == []
             assert res.clock_held[tid] == ("review_provider_wall", RESET)
+            assert res.respawn_guarded == [(tid, "review_provider_wall")]
             task = kb.get_task(conn, tid)
             assert task.status == lane and not task.claim_lock
             assert task.consecutive_failures == 0
